    "id": "bihar-approves-10mw-solar-power-plant-on-son-canal",
    "title": "Bihar approves 10MW solar power plant on Son Canal.",
    "summary": "Solar Revolution in Bihar: Son Canal to Power the Future with 10MW Clean Energy Project When Sunlight Meets Water: Bihar’s Bold Energy Leap Imagine canals that don’t just carry water—but also carry the future of energy. That vision is now becoming real in Bihar. The state is stepping into a new era where sunlight and [...]",
    "content": "Solar Revolution in Bihar: Son Canal to Power the Future with 10MW Clean Energy Project\n\nWhen Sunlight Meets Water: Bihar’s Bold Energy Leap\n\nImagine canals that don’t just carry water—but also carry the future of energy. That vision is now becoming real in Bihar. The state is stepping into a new era where sunlight and infrastructure work together to power millions of lives.\n\nNow, the government has approved a 10MW solar power plant on the embankment of the Western Son Canal. This is not just a project. It is a shift in thinking.\n\nMoreover, this initiative blends innovation with sustainability. As a result, Bihar is moving closer to energy independence while protecting its environment.\n\nProject Details: Where Innovation Takes Shape\n\nThe plan focuses on the first one-kilometer stretch of the canal. Around 80,000 square feet of space will host modern solar panels.\n\nAdditionally, the state power company will build and operate the plant directly. This ensures faster execution and better control.\n\nImportantly, the Water Resources Department has already granted the NOC. Therefore, the tender process is expected to begin soon.\n\nFurthermore, this model solves a major problem—land scarcity. Instead of acquiring new land, Bihar is optimizing existing canal infrastructure.\n\nSafety First: Protecting Canal Infrastructure\n\nWhile the project is ambitious, safety remains a top priority. Authorities have clearly instructed that the canal embankments must remain strong.\n\nTherefore, engineers will design the installation carefully. They will ensure zero damage to the structure.\n\nAt the same time, continuous monitoring will help maintain both energy output and structural safety.\n\nGreen Bihar Vision: Clean Energy, Cleaner Future\n\nThis project strongly supports Bihar’s environmental goals. It aligns perfectly with the state’s “Jal-Jeevan-Hariyali” mission.\n\nAs a result, the plant will reduce carbon emissions significantly. It will also promote renewable energy adoption across the region.\n\nMoreover, local areas will benefit from stable voltage and improved electricity supply. This will directly impact homes, farms, and small businesses.\n\nA Pilot That Can Transform Bihar\n\nInterestingly, this is just the beginning. The Son Canal project will act as a pilot model.\n\nIf successful, similar solar installations may appear along Kosi and Gandak canals. Consequently, Bihar could develop a vast solar network across its waterways.\n\nIn addition, this approach can inspire other Indian states to rethink energy infrastructure.\n\nWhy This Matters for Bihar’s Future\n\nThis project is more than electricity generation. It represents:\n\nSmarter use of public infrastructure\n\nFaster transition to renewable energy\n\nReduced dependency on traditional power sources\n\nStronger rural electrification\n\nTherefore, Bihar is not just solving today’s problems. It is preparing for tomorrow.\n\nBe Part of Bihar’s Transformation\n\nStories like these are reshaping how the world sees Bihar. And this is just one of many powerful changes happening on the ground.\n\n👉 Follow www.biharsay.com for more such regular updates and become part of the 13K+ global community!\n\nBihar Say is Bihar’s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform. It is reshaping the state’s image through impactful stories on culture, business, and grassroots change.\n\nWith 13,000+ followers, top LinkedIn impressions, and partnerships with platforms like DailyHunt, Bihar Say stands as the digital voice of Bihar.\n\n🎙️ Don’t miss BiharCast—its flagship podcast uncovering untold stories and rising voices from the heart of Bihar.",
