    "id": "pm-kisan-samman-nidhi-how-digital-reform-can-empower-every-farmer",
    "title": "PM-Kisan Samman Nidhi: How Digital Reform Can Empower Every Farmer",
    "summary": "PM-Kisan Samman Nidhi: How Digital Reforms Can Unlock Benefits for Every Farmer When policy intent meets ground realities, meaningful change becomes possible. For India’s small and marginal farmers, the PM-Kisan Samman Nidhi Yojana continues to be a strong pillar of financial support.Every instalment brings stability, confidence, and dignity. However, as India accelerates toward digital governance, [...]",
    "content": "PM-Kisan Samman Nidhi: How Digital Reforms Can Unlock Benefits for Every Farmer\n\nWhen policy intent meets ground realities, meaningful change becomes possible.\n\nFor India’s small and marginal farmers, the PM-Kisan Samman Nidhi Yojana continues to be a strong pillar of financial support.Every instalment brings stability, confidence, and dignity.\n\nHowever, as India accelerates toward digital governance, a new opportunity has emerged.By aligning old land records with modern systems, the scheme can reach every eligible farmer without delay.\n\nPM-Kisan Samman Nidhi: A Strong Scheme with Growing Reach\n\nThe Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi scheme already supports crores of farmers nationwide.It delivers direct income support and reduces dependency on informal credit.\n\nImportantly, the government has strengthened transparency through digital verification.As a result, leakages have reduced and delivery has improved.\n\nNow, the next step is inclusion.\n\nBridging the Gap Between Old Land Records and New Technology\n\nAcross rural India, many farmers hold land recorded in traditional registers such as Gunj-Bahis and measurement books.These records reflect genuine ownership passed down through generations.\n\nHowever, many of them are not yet digitised.Therefore, online systems sometimes fail to capture this reality.\n\nOnce these records enter digital databases, thousands of farmers will benefit instantly.\n\nWhy the ‘Fard’ Requirement Can Become a Gateway, Not a Barrier\n\nThe mandatory land fard aims to ensure accuracy and fairness.That intent is positive and necessary.\n\nAt the same time, many farmers need support to obtain this document.With faster processing and flexible verification, the same rule can empower farmers.\n\nThus, reform—not rollback—is the real solution.\n\nLocal Leadership Showing the Way Forward\n\nIn Biraul block of Darbhanga, Bihar, constructive dialogue has already begun.Block Chief Mamta Devi has highlighted practical solutions to state authorities.\n\nOut of 12,566 PM-Kisan beneficiaries, nearly 1,200 farmers rely on legacy land records.Their cases are genuine and verifiable.\n\nWith targeted drives, their inclusion can happen smoothly.\n\nSmart Solutions That Can Strengthen PM-Kisan Further\n\nSeveral positive steps can accelerate impact:\n\nDigitising old registries through special campaigns\n\nAccepting verified legacy documents temporarily\n\nSpeeding up mutation and fard issuance\n\nEnabling alternative farmer verification methods\n\nTogether, these measures can make PM-Kisan more inclusive.\n\nA Moment to Strengthen Trust Between Farmers and the System\n\nDigital India works best when technology adapts to people—not the other way around.By integrating history with innovation, governance becomes humane.\n\nPM-Kisan already has the foundation.Now, thoughtful execution can complete the vision.\n\nStay Updated with Stories That Drive Positive Change\n\nFor stories that highlight solutions, progress, and grassroots voices, stay connected.\n\n👉 Follow www.biharsay.com for regular updates🌍 Join 13,000+ readers worldwide\n\nBihar Say is Bihar’s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, reshaping perceptions through impactful narratives on culture, business, governance, and change.With partnerships like DailyHunt and the flagship BiharCast podcast, Bihar Say continues to amplify Bihar’s real stories—responsibly and positively.\n\nViral Positive Headlines (Options)\n\nPM-Kisan and the Path Forward: Turning Digital Challenges into Farmer Opportunity\n\nStrengthening PM-Kisan: Why Updating Land Records Can Transform Rural India",
