    "id": "worlds-largest-shivlinga-reaches-bihar-gopalganj-to-virat-ramayan-mandir",
    "title": "World’s Largest Shivlinga Reaches Bihar | Gopalganj to Virat Ramayan Mandir",
    "summary": "From Stone to Soul: The World’s Largest Shivlinga Enters Bihar, Carrying Faith on 96 Wheels When faith moves, even roads make way.And this time, devotion arrived on 96 wheels, carrying the world’s largest Shivlinga into Bihar. A Historic Moment for Bihar’s Spiritual Landscape Bihar witnessed a rare spiritual milestone.The world’s largest Shivlinga entered Gopalganj district, [...]",
    "content": "From Stone to Soul: The World’s Largest Shivlinga Enters Bihar, Carrying Faith on 96 Wheels\n\nWhen faith moves, even roads make way.And this time, devotion arrived on 96 wheels, carrying the world’s largest Shivlinga into Bihar.\n\nA Historic Moment for Bihar’s Spiritual Landscape\n\nBihar witnessed a rare spiritual milestone.The world’s largest Shivlinga entered Gopalganj district, drawing crowds, chants, and deep emotion.\n\nAs soon as the Shivlinga crossed into Bihar, devotion filled the air.Meanwhile, devotees lined the roads with flowers and folded hands.At the same time, chants of “Har Har Mahadev” echoed across towns.\n\nNotably, district officials and police officers also joined the rituals.They offered flowers, sandalwood, and prayers.Therefore, the moment turned administrative presence into collective devotion.\n\nA 210-Metric-Ton Marvel on a Special 96-Wheel Truck\n\nMoving such faith required extraordinary engineering.Hence, authorities used a specially designed 96-wheel truck.\n\nThe Shivlinga weighs 210 metric tons.Because of this, engineers planned every turn carefully.As a result, the journey remained slow but steady.\n\nThe convoy will complete the Gopalganj stretch within 48 to 50 hours.After that, it will move toward East Champaran.Along the route, people continue to gather for darshan and a glimpse.\n\nCrafted from a Single Stone: The Art Behind the Shivlinga\n\nWhat makes this Shivlinga truly exceptional?It comes from Mahabalipuram, Tamil Nadu, a global heritage hub.\n\nArtisans sculpted it from one massive granite stone.Therefore, no joints or segments exist.This single-stone design reflects rare Indian craftsmanship.\n\nMoreover, the Shivlinga showcases traditional South Indian carving styles.Every curve speaks of patience, devotion, and mastery.\n\nAccording to Vinayak Venkataraman, founder of the manufacturing company,the project cost nearly ₹3 crore.Clearly, it stands as both art and offering.\n\nWhy Gopalganj Became a Sacred Stop\n\nGopalganj did not just witness movement.Instead, it became a moment of pause and prayer.\n\nLocals waited for hours along highways.Women performed aarti.Children showered petals.Elders folded hands in silence.\n\nConsequently, roads turned into corridors of devotion.Faith, once again, united strangers.\n\nThe Shivlinga’s Final Destination: Virat Ramayan Mandir\n\nThis sacred journey has a powerful purpose.The Shivlinga will be installed at the Virat Ramayan Mandir in East Champaran.\n\nThe temple project was initiated by Kishore Kunal,Chairman, Bihar State Religious Trust Board,and a key figure of Mahavir Mandir Nyas Samiti.\n\nThe temple’s scale reflects its vision.It will stretch 1080 feet in length and 540 feet in width.\n\nSince the foundation stone was laid on 20 June 2023,several structures are already complete.These include the entrance gate, Singh Dwar, Nandi Mandap, and Garbhagriha piling.\n\nIf timelines hold,the Shivlinga will be installed by February, welcoming the new year with divine energy.\n\nMore Than a Structure, A Statement of Bihar’s Rising Identity\n\nThis moment goes beyond religion.It reflects Bihar’s growing presence on the national spiritual map.\n\nMoreover, it bridges South Indian craftsmanship with Eastern devotion.Thus, culture travels.Faith connects.And Bihar stands at the center.\n\nStay Connected to Stories That Shape Bihar\n\nFor more such powerful stories from Bihar’s heartlands,👉 Follow www.biharsay.com\n\nBecome part of our 13,000+ global community that believes in facts, culture, and grassroots narratives.\n\nBihar Say is Bihar’s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform,reshaping the state’s image through stories of culture, business, and change.\n\nWith strong reach on LinkedIn and partnerships with platforms like DailyHunt,Bihar Say stands as the digital voice of Bihar.\n\nIts flagship podcast and video series, BiharCast,dives into untold stories, changemakers, and rising voices—straight from the heart of Bihar.",
