    "id": "patna-to-delhi-kolkata-train-fare-increased",
    "title": "Patna to Delhi & Kolkata Train Fare Increased",
    "summary": "Train Fare Shock for Bihar Travelers: Patna to Delhi & Kolkata Just Got Costlier—Check New Ticket Prices A simple train journey from Patna just became heavier on your pocket.And if Delhi or Kolkata is your next stop, this update matters right now. Indian Railways has announced a fresh fare hike.As a result, premium train travel [...]",
    "content": "Train Fare Shock for Bihar Travelers: Patna to Delhi & Kolkata Just Got Costlier—Check New Ticket Prices\n\nA simple train journey from Patna just became heavier on your pocket.And if Delhi or Kolkata is your next stop, this update matters right now.\n\nIndian Railways has announced a fresh fare hike.As a result, premium train travel from Bihar will now cost more.Moreover, the change takes effect immediately.\n\nPremium Train Fare Hike: What Changed and Why It Matters\n\nIndian Railways has increased fares for premium category trains.Therefore, passengers traveling from Patna to Delhi and Kolkata will feel the impact first.\n\nAccording to officials, new ticket rates came into force from today.Consequently, Bihar’s busiest routes now reflect higher prices.Most importantly, sleeper and AC passengers will pay more than before.\n\nPatna to Kolkata: New Train Ticket Prices Explained\n\nIf you travel frequently to Kolkata, note these changes carefully.\n\nSleeper Class: ₹350 → ₹360\n\n3E Economy AC: ₹845 → ₹855\n\n3AC: ₹915 → ₹925\n\n2AC: ₹1275 → ₹1285\n\n1AC: ₹2115 → ₹2125\n\nMeanwhile, other classes saw a ₹5 hike.Thus, even budget travelers will notice the difference.\n\nPatna to Delhi: Travel Will Cost Even More\n\nTraveling from Patna to New Delhi now demands a bigger budget.\n\nSleeper & AC Classes: +₹20\n\nOther Classes: +₹10\n\nAdditionally, Jan Shatabdi Express AC Chair Car fare rose from ₹805 to ₹815.As a result, frequent commuters will feel the pinch faster.\n\nWhy Indian Railways Raised Fares\n\nRailway officials aim to balance service quality and operational costs.Therefore, premium routes saw the first revision.However, officials confirmed that ordinary tickets remain unaffected.\n\nStill, passengers must plan journeys more carefully now.\n\nOTP-Based Ticket Booking: A Big Shift Begins\n\nAlongside the fare hike, Railways introduced a One-Time Password (OTP) system.This move focuses on secure and transparent ticket booking.\n\nCurrently, OTP verification applies to over 100 major trains, including:\n\nRajdhani-linked routes\n\nPatna–Kota\n\nAra–Durg\n\nRajendra Nagar–Howrah\n\nDanapur–Secunderabad\n\nPurva Express\n\nThus, fraudulent bookings may soon reduce significantly.\n\nOTP System to Expand Across Danapur Division\n\nSources confirm further expansion soon.Now, Railways plan to implement OTP booking on all express trains passing through Patna Junction and Danapur Division.\n\nOfficials are preparing a complete train list.Meanwhile, passengers will receive OTPs during booking.Only after verification will tickets be confirmed.\n\nHowever, this rule will not apply to:\n\nAdvance reservations\n\nGeneral unreserved tickets\n\nThe official rollout date will be announced shortly.\n\nWhy This Matters for Bihar Passengers\n\nTogether, fare hikes and OTP verification signal a new railway phase.On one hand, travel costs rise.On the other, booking transparency improves.\n\nTherefore, passengers must stay informed to avoid last-minute surprises.\n\n🔔 Final CTA (No Conclusion as Requested)\n\nFor daily Bihar train updates, verified news, and ground-level stories that matter—👉 Follow www.biharsay.com\n\nJoin a 13,000+ strong global community that trusts Bihar Say,Bihar’s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, reshaping the state’s image through culture, business, transport, and grassroots change.\n\nWith top LinkedIn impressions, partnerships with DailyHunt, and flagship shows like BiharCast, Bihar Say is the digital voice of Bihar—from its stations to its stories.",
