    "id": "over-1000-civil-servants-compete-in-national-athletics-championship-in-patna",
    "title": "Over 1,000 Civil Servants Compete in National Athletics Championship in Patna",
    "summary": "When Bureaucrats Turn Athletes: Patna Hosts India’s Largest Civil Services Sports Showdown At sunrise in Patna, track spikes replaced office shoes as India’s bureaucracy sprinted toward a different kind of finish line. From December 13 to 15, 2025, Patna became the beating heart of Indian sports administration. Over 1,000 civil servants gathered not for files [...]",
    "content": "When Bureaucrats Turn Athletes: Patna Hosts India’s Largest Civil Services Sports Showdown\n\nAt sunrise in Patna, track spikes replaced office shoes as India’s bureaucracy sprinted toward a different kind of finish line.\n\nFrom December 13 to 15, 2025, Patna became the beating heart of Indian sports administration. Over 1,000 civil servants gathered not for files or meetings, but for competition, fitness, and national pride.\n\nA Rare National Sporting Convergence in Patna\n\nThe All India Civil Services Athletics Championship 2025–26 is unfolding at the iconic Patliputra Sports Complex. Notably, 1,084 participants have travelled from every corner of the country.\n\nThis includes 702 men, 328 women, and 54 officials. Moreover, athletes represent 28 states and nine Union Territories, such as Haryana, Gujarat, Uttar Pradesh, Maharashtra, Tamil Nadu, and Kerala.\n\nAs a result, Patna has transformed into a truly national sporting arena.\n\nHigh-Speed Races Meet World-Class Facilities\n\nFrom the very first morning, energy filled the air. Athletes charged through events like the 100 metres and 400 metres, testing speed and stamina.\n\nMeanwhile, the synthetic track and international-standard field facilities ensured fairness and precision. Therefore, competitors performed at a truly professional level.\n\nAdditionally, events span sprints, middle-distance races, high jump, long jump, shot put, discus, javelin, and relay races. Each discipline highlights discipline, focus, and years of dedication.\n\nVeterans Prove Age Is Just a Number\n\nImportantly, the championship goes beyond youth.\n\nAthletes aged 40 to 60 are competing in specially designed veterans’ categories. Consequently, experience now runs alongside youthful energy.\n\nThis inclusion sends a strong message. Fitness has no expiry date. Commitment matters more than age.\n\nBihar’s Sports Vision Takes Center Stage\n\nSpeaking at the event, Bihar Chief Secretary Pratyay Amrit (Tag: Pratyay Amrit) expressed pride in hosting the championship.\n\n“It is a matter of honour for Bihar to host this national-level athletics championship,” he said.\n\nHe also highlighted that every participant is a serving government official who continues to pursue sport despite demanding careers. Therefore, the championship stands as proof that public service and personal fitness can grow together.\n\nWhy This Event Matters Beyond the Track\n\nSince the formation of a separate Sports Department in 2024, Bihar has accelerated its sports roadmap.\n\nAs a result:\n\nNational and international events now choose Bihar\n\nDistrict-level sports academies are expanding\n\nYouth participation is steadily rising\n\nMoreover, such championships boost sports tourism. Visiting athletes explore the city, interact with locals, and carry Bihar’s story back home.\n\nIn other words, every runner here becomes an ambassador for the state.\n\nPatna’s Moment on the National Sports Map\n\nOnce known mainly for history and governance, Patna is now carving a new identity.\n\nThrough events like this, the city proves it can host large-scale national championships with professionalism and warmth. Consequently, Bihar’s sporting narrative is changing—fast and visibly.\n\nStay Connected to Bihar’s Real Stories\n\nWant more such powerful, human stories from Bihar?\n\n👉 Follow www.biharsay.com for regular, credible updates🌍 Become part of a 13,000+ strong global community\n\nBihar Say is Bihar’s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, reshaping the state’s image through impactful narratives on culture, business, sports, and grassroots change.\n\nWith top LinkedIn impressions for Bihar-focused content, partnerships with platforms like DailyHunt, and the flagship BiharCast podcast & video series, Bihar Say is the digital voice of Bihar—straight from the ground, straight to the world.",
