    "id": "purnea-airport-to-connect-with-nh-31committee-formed-for-dpr",
    "title": "Purnea Airport to Connect with NH-31:Committee Formed for DPR",
    "summary": "Purnea Airport’s Highway Boost: How NH-31 Connectivity Could Change North Bihar’s Growth Story  When a Highway Meets a Runway, a Region Takes Off What happens when a highway meets an airport?In Purnea, it signals momentum, mobility, and a powerful push toward regional growth. On December 11, 2025, the Bihar administration took a decisive step.It initiated [...]",
    "content": "Purnea Airport’s Highway Boost: How NH-31 Connectivity Could Change North Bihar’s Growth Story\n\nWhen a Highway Meets a Runway, a Region Takes Off\n\nWhat happens when a highway meets an airport?In Purnea, it signals momentum, mobility, and a powerful push toward regional growth.\n\nOn December 11, 2025, the Bihar administration took a decisive step.It initiated the process to link Purnea Airport with National Highway-31.As a result, connectivity in North Bihar could soon change forever.\n\nThe move gained clarity after a high-level review meeting.District Magistrate Anshul Kumar chaired the session.Moreover, officials from the Airport Authority of India (AAI) joined the discussion.\n\nWhy NH-31 Connectivity Matters for Purnea\n\nNH-31 serves as a vital economic corridor.Therefore, linking it directly to Purnea Airport strengthens regional access.\n\nAt present, airport connectivity limits travel efficiency.However, the new road link could reduce delays significantly.In addition, it may boost tourism, trade, and emergency mobility.\n\nMost importantly, North Bihar gains smoother access to national air routes.Consequently, businesses and investors may look at Purnea differently.\n\nCommittee Formed to Drive the DPR Process\n\nTo ensure structured execution, the administration formed a multi-departmental committee.This committee will oversee surveys, planning, and coordination.\n\nThe Executive Engineer, Purnea Road Division, received clear instructions.He must submit a detailed survey report for the proposed link road.Meanwhile, the committee will monitor progress at every stage.\n\nCommittee Members Include\n\nSub-Divisional Officer (Sadar)\n\nExecutive Engineer, Road Division\n\nMunicipal Commissioner, Purnea\n\nChief Security Officer, Purnea Airport\n\nCircle Officer, K Nagar\n\nDistrict Land Acquisition Officer\n\nTogether, they will streamline approvals and execution.\n\nLand Acquisition and Defence Coordination\n\nThe project requires 15.99 acres of land.This land will support the airport’s approach lighting system.\n\nTherefore, the DM directed officials to compile all acquisition data quickly.However, final action depends on Ministry of Defence approval.\n\nIn addition, coordination with Chunapur Air Force Station is mandatory.The administration will engage directly with the Station Commander.This step ensures both civilian and defence safety protocols align.\n\nFirefighting and Aviation Safety Measures\n\nSafety remained a key focus during the meeting.Hence, the DM issued firm instructions to the District Fire Officer.\n\nFirefighting staff must be deployed at the Air Force airport when required.If shortages arise, local replacements must step in immediately.\n\nFurthermore, AAI will fund specialised training for fire personnel.Drivers of fire vehicles will also receive local training.This process will happen in coordination with the District Transport Officer.\n\nMedical and Emergency Preparedness at the Airport\n\nMedical readiness received equal priority.Accordingly, the Civil Surgeon of Purnea received specific directions.\n\nMedical officers, paramedical staff, and ambulances will remain available.This applies to both Chunapur Airport and the interim terminal building.\n\nAdditionally, officials will maintain a clear duty roster.This step ensures accountability and round-the-clock emergency care.\n\nWildlife Control and Civil Defence Support\n\nBird and animal movement near runways poses serious risks.Therefore, Civil Defence volunteers will manage wildlife control.\n\nThe SDO (Sadar) and Deputy Controller of Civil Defence received instructions.They must release one month’s honorarium to the volunteers promptly.\n\nMeanwhile, the Director of the interim terminal must ensure funds flow on time.This coordination reduces operational risks significantly.\n\nWhat This Means for North Bihar\n\nThis initiative goes beyond road construction.Instead, it reflects Bihar’s evolving infrastructure mindset.\n\nBetter airport access means faster movement.Moreover, it strengthens disaster response capacity.At the same time, it unlocks economic and tourism opportunities.\n\nFor Purnea, this link could redefine its regional importance.\n\nStay Connected to Bihar’s Fast-Changing Story\n\nFor more such credible, timely, and human-centred updates, follow www.biharsay.com and become part of our 13,000+ global community 🌍\n\nBihar Say is Bihar’s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, reshaping the state’s image through impactful stories on culture, business, infrastructure, and grassroots change.With strong reach on LinkedIn, partnerships with platforms like DailyHunt, and our flagship podcast BiharCast, we amplify voices from the heart of Bihar.\n\n👉 Follow www.biharsay.com and stay ahead of Bihar’s growth narrative.",
