    "id": "bihar-cabinet-approves-creation-of-three-new-departments",
    "title": "Bihar cabinet approves creation of three new departments",
    "summary": "Bihar Just Hit the Reset Button — And 1 Crore Youth Are at the Heart of It! Bihar has taken a bold step, and the energy is unmistakable. The state government has approved three new departments to fast-track jobs, boost higher education, and strengthen its fast-growing aviation sector. This is not just policy work. This [...]",
    "content": "Bihar Just Hit the Reset Button — And 1 Crore Youth Are at the Heart of It!\n\nBihar has taken a bold step, and the energy is unmistakable. The state government has approved three new departments to fast-track jobs, boost higher education, and strengthen its fast-growing aviation sector. This is not just policy work. This is a generational shift for Bihar’s youth.\n\nA Big Leap Toward Jobs, Skills, and Growth\n\nThe Bihar Cabinet, chaired by Chief Minister Nitish Kumar, cleared 19 major decisions on December 9. Among them, the biggest highlight was the creation of three new departments — a move aimed at hitting the target of one crore employment opportunities in the next five years.\n\nAccording to Arvind Kumar Chaudhary, Additional Chief Secretary of the Cabinet Secretariat Department, these departments will directly improve implementation speed and policy impact.\n\nAnd the names say it all:\n\nYouth, Employment & Skill Development\n\nHigher Education\n\nCivil Aviation\n\nEach department carries a clear mission. The first will push skill development aggressively so young people can step into better opportunities. The second will improve the quality of higher education. The third will support Bihar’s expanding aviation infrastructure as air travel demand rises.\n\nTogether, they form a blueprint for a more capable and confident Bihar.\n\nA New Identity for Key Departments\n\nThe changes did not stop with the creation of new wings. The cabinet also renamed several existing departments to match Bihar’s present needs.\n\nHere are the major updates:\n\nThe Animal & Fisheries Resources Department will now operate as the Dairy, Fisheries and Animal Resources Department.\n\nThe Labour Resources Department is now the Labour Resources and Migrant Workers Welfare Department.\n\nThe Art, Culture and Youth Department will now function as the Art and Culture Department.\n\nAdditionally, the industries department received a major upgrade as the Directorate of Technical Development officially became the Directorate of Micro, Small & Medium Enterprise (MSME). This step aims to boost MSMEs so they can compete globally.\n\nEach renaming carries a larger message — Bihar is aligning itself with new economic realities.\n\nFinancial Decisions That Impact Thousands\n\nThe cabinet also approved a much-awaited update for government employees and pensioners. With immediate effect, the state increased the Dearness Allowance (DA) by:\n\n5% for 6th Pay Commission beneficiaries (from 252% to 257%)\n\n8% for 5th Pay Commission beneficiaries (from 466% to 474%)\n\nThese revised rates apply from July 1, 2025, and they offer significant financial relief.\n\nIn another key decision, the cabinet sanctioned ₹400 crore for clearing the electricity dues of all urban local bodies owed to North and South Bihar Power Distribution Companies. This move is expected to strengthen local governance and improve service stability.\n\nStrategic Steps for Safety, Education, and Empowerment\n\nTwo districts — Gaya Ji and Munger — are now officially Civil Defence Districts. The decision includes the creation of 14 new posts to support better disaster management, security planning, and emergency readiness.\n\nAdditionally, the cabinet approved:\n\nAppointment of Mohammad Imdad Raza, son of BSF Sub-Inspector Late Mohammad Imtiyaz, who was martyred during Operation Sindoor.\n\nAn MoU between Bihar’s Finance Department and National Stock Exchange of India Limited (NSEIL). This partnership will run a Student Skilling Programme to empower youth with financial and technical knowledge.\n\nEach step points toward a stronger state machinery, better welfare, and a more future-ready generation.\n\nBihar Is Changing — And Its Youth Are Leading the Charge\n\nFrom aviation and education to MSMEs and disaster response, Bihar is pushing forward with a clear vision. Most importantly, the state is creating an environment where young people can dream big and succeed at home.\n\nThis is the Bihar we always wanted to see — faster, sharper, and more determined.\n\n👉 For more inspiring, apolitical stories and development updates from Bihar, follow www.biharsay.com and join our global 13k+ community!Bihar Say is Bihar’s leading storytelling platform, reshaping the state’s image through powerful narratives, impact stories, and voices from the heart of Bihar.Be part of the change. Be part of the movement.",
