    "id": "extra-coaches-added-on-delhi-bound-bihar-trains-amid-indigo-crisis",
    "title": "Extra Coaches Added on Delhi-Bound Bihar Trains amid Indigo Crisis",
    "summary": "Indigo Crisis Impact: Bihar Steps Up With Extra Coaches on Delhi-Bound Trains | A Big Relief for Stranded Flyers When flights stop, hopes often sink. But this week, Bihar turned panic into relief with quick decisions that helped thousands of travellers stuck due to the ongoing Indigo crisis. For many, trains became the lifeline they [...]",
    "content": "Indigo Crisis Impact: Bihar Steps Up With Extra Coaches on Delhi-Bound Trains | A Big Relief for Stranded Flyers\n\nWhen flights stop, hopes often sink. But this week, Bihar turned panic into relief with quick decisions that helped thousands of travellers stuck due to the ongoing Indigo crisis. For many, trains became the lifeline they desperately needed.\n\nWhy the Indigo Crisis Created Chaos for Travellers\n\nThe sudden wave of Indigo flight cancellations left passengers confused and stressed. Many of them had urgent plans, medical needs or office commitments in Delhi. As chaos grew, people started crowding airports and searching for alternatives.Yet, travelling by train seemed impossible due to packed waiting lists.\n\nThis is where the Indian Railways stepped in.And the move changed everything.\n\nRailways Add Extra Coaches to Key Delhi-Bound Trains\n\nTo ease the pressure, East Central Railway (ECR) acted fast on the instructions of the Danapur Division. Their quick response restored confidence among the stranded passengers.\n\nOfficials, including Saraswati Chandra, Chief Public Relations Officer of ECR (@RailMinIndia), confirmed the steps.\n\nExtra Coaches Added:\n\nTejas Rajdhani Express – One extra Third AC coach\n\nSampoorna Kranti Express – One extra Second AC coach\n\nThese additions increased seat availability within hours. As a result, people finally found a reliable option to reach Delhi without panic.\n\nSpecial Trains Flagged Off for Immediate Relief\n\nBesides adding coaches, Railways launched several special trains to handle the sudden surge in demand. These trains ensured that stranded flyers did not have to wait endlessly.\n\nHere are the key special trains running to and from Delhi:\n\n02309 Patna → Anand Vihar Terminal SpecialDeparts: 8 December, 20:30Arrives: Next day, 15:00\n\n02310 Anand Vihar → Patna SpecialDeparts: 7 & 9 December, 19:00Arrives: Next day, 14:00\n\n02395 Patna → Anand Vihar SpecialDeparts: 7 December, 20:30Arrives: Next day, 15:00\n\n02396 Anand Vihar → Patna SpecialDeparts: 8 December, 19:00Arrives: Next day, 14:00\n\n05563 Darbhanga → Anand Vihar SpecialDeparts: 7 December, 18:15Arrives: Next day, 21:15\n\n05564 Anand Vihar → Darbhanga SpecialDeparts: 9 December, 00:05Arrives: 23:00\n\nThese services created breathing room for passengers, especially those who lost their travel plans due to cancelled @IndiGo6E flights.\n\nWhy This Move Matters for Bihar and Delhi Travelers\n\nThe Indigo disruption exposed how fragile travel networks can be. Yet, the railways showed that strong systems can absorb shocks when quick actions are taken.Furthermore, this step proved that Bihar handles crises with clarity and compassion.\n\nPassengers now see a clear path forward. They have trains, seats and timely alternatives. Even though the airline crisis continues, people can still move toward safety, work and family.\n\nStay Updated With Bihar’s Fastest-Growing News Community\n\nFor more such important and timely updates that impact your travel, safety and daily life, follow:\n\n👉 www.biharsay.comJoin our 13,000+ global community and be a part of Bihar’s most trusted apolitical storytelling platform.Bihar Say continues to reshape Bihar’s identity through stories of culture, development and change.Don’t miss the next update—become part of the journey today.",
