    "id": "bihar-cabinet-ministers-list-2025-names-parties-roles-explained",
    "title": "Bihar Cabinet Ministers List 2025 – Names, Parties & Roles Explained",
    "summary": "Meet the Power Players: Bihar’s New 2025 Cabinet Ministers and What Their Roles Mean for You” Bihar’s New Cabinet: A Fresh Chapter After the 2025 Mandate This year, the National Democratic Alliance (NDA) delivered a resounding victory in Bihar — winning 202 out of 243 seats. With such a mandate, Nitish Kumar, under the banner [...]",
    "content": "Meet the Power Players: Bihar’s New 2025 Cabinet Ministers and What Their Roles Mean for You”\n\nBihar’s New Cabinet: A Fresh Chapter After the 2025 Mandate\n\nThis year, the National Democratic Alliance (NDA) delivered a resounding victory in Bihar — winning 202 out of 243 seats. With such a mandate, Nitish Kumar, under the banner of Janata Dal (United), has returned as Chief Minister, supported strongly by the BJP and its alliance partners. This cabinet isn’t just a collection of names; it signals the direction Bihar plans to take in development, welfare, and governance.\n\nWhy This Cabinet Formation Matters\n\nWhen a new cabinet is sworn in, it reflects the priorities of the government. Who gets which portfolio is not random — it’s a deliberate choice. Through these assignments, we see how the ruling alliance plans to deliver on infrastructure, employment, welfare, and more. In Bihar’s case, the mix of experience, youth, and regional representation in the cabinet tells us a lot about the political strategy and the roadmap for the next term.\n\nMoreover, understanding who holds which position gives citizens clarity — knowing who is responsible for education, health, revenue, or rural development empowers them to stay informed, ask relevant questions, and hold leaders accountable.\n\nMeet the Ministers: The 2025 Bihar Cabinet List\n\nHere’s a breakdown of the 25 cabinet ministers in Bihar, including Chief Minister Nitish Kumar, along with their political parties:\n\nNo.\nName\nParty\n\n1\nNitish Kumar (Chief Minister)\nJD(U)\n\n2\nAshok Choudhary\nJD(U)\n\n3\nMohammad Zama Khan\nJD(U)\n\n4\nLesi Singh\nJD(U)\n\n5\nMadan Sahni\nJD(U)\n\n6\nSunil Kumar\nJD(U)\n\n7\nVijay Kumar Choudhary\nJD(U)\n\n8\nBijendra Prasad Yadav\nJD(U)\n\n9\nShravan Kumar\nJD(U)\n\n10\nVijay Kumar Sinha\nBJP\n\n11\nSamrat Choudhary\nBJP\n\n12\nDilip Kumar Jaiswal\nBJP\n\n13\nMangal Pandey\nBJP\n\n14\nRam Kripal Yadav\nBJP\n\n15\nSanjay Singh Tiger\nBJP\n\n16\nArun Shankar Prasad\nBJP\n\n17\nSurendra Prasad Mehta\nBJP\n\n18\nNarayan Prasad\nBJP\n\n19\nRama Nishad\nBJP\n\n20\nLakhendra Kumar Roshan\nBJP\n\n21\nShreyashi Singh\nBJP\n\n22\nPramod Kumar\nBJP\n\n23\nNitin Nabin\nBJP\n\n24\nSantosh Kumar Suman\nHAM(S)\n\n25\nSanjay Kumar\nLJP (RV)\n\n26\nDeepak Prakash\nRLM\n\nThis list reflects a strong BJP presence, showing where the real political power within the NDA lies.\n\nKey Leaders & Power Centers in the New Government\n\nNitish Kumar remains at the helm, bringing his decades of political experience.\n\nSamrat Choudhary and Vijay Kumar Sinha, both from BJP, are major figures as they take top ministerial roles.\n\nOn the JD(U) side, leaders like Ashok Choudhary, Madan Sahni, and Bijendra Yadav bring continuity and stability.\n\nMeanwhile, smaller alliance partners like HAM(S) and LJP (RV) also get representation, ensuring a broader base.\n\nThis spread demonstrates the NDA’s balancing act — it rewards loyalty, maintains strong BJP influence, and keeps key regional partners engaged.\n\nWhat This Cabinet Means for Bihar’s Future\n\nDevelopment Focus: With strong leadership from both JD(U) and BJP, the cabinet is poised to push aggressive infrastructure and welfare projects.\n\nWelfare & Social Equity: The inclusion of leaders from varied social backgrounds suggests a government that remains committed to social welfare.\n\nPolitical Stability: With a clear majority, the NDA-led government doesn’t just have numbers; it has a team that appears stable and united.\n\nAccountability: Knowing exactly who handles what portfolio empowers citizens to demand transparency and action.\n\nUltimately, this cabinet isn’t just about political power — it’s about shaping Bihar’s future.\n\nWhy You Should Stay Updated\n\nStaying informed about Bihar’s ministerial lineup is more than politics — it’s about understanding who will decide your education, health, infrastructure, and job opportunities. As this government implements its vision, these ministers will directly influence how policies impact people’s everyday lives.\n\nTo stay on top of the latest developments, follow BiharSay.com. As Bihar’s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, we reshape our state’s image through powerful narratives on culture, business, and grassroots change. Join our 13,000+ global community for real-time updates, deep analysis, and inspiring stories.",
