    "id": "assembly-elections-bihar-set-for-vote-counting-tomorrow-across-46-centres-in-38-districts",
    "title": "Assembly Elections: Bihar set for Vote Counting tomorrow across 46 centres in 38 districts",
    "summary": "All Eyes on Bihar: Vote Counting Begins Tomorrow Across 46 Centres — A Historic Election Awaits Its Verdict! Bihar Awaits Its Big Verdict The air in Bihar is thick with anticipation. After weeks of campaigning, two phases of voting, and record-breaking participation, the Assembly Election results are just hours away. From Patna to Purnea, people [...]",
    "content": "All Eyes on Bihar: Vote Counting Begins Tomorrow Across 46 Centres — A Historic Election Awaits Its Verdict!\n\nBihar Awaits Its Big Verdict\n\nThe air in Bihar is thick with anticipation. After weeks of campaigning, two phases of voting, and record-breaking participation, the Assembly Election results are just hours away. From Patna to Purnea, people are waiting eagerly as counting begins tomorrow at 8 AM across 46 centres in 38 districts.\n\nThis year’s election is not just another political event — it’s a landmark in Bihar’s democratic journey. With an impressive 67.13% voter turnout, the state has witnessed its highest-ever polling percentage since 1951. The enthusiasm reflects the citizens’ growing trust in democracy and their desire for change.\n\nInside the Nerve Centre of Democracy\n\nAt the heart of this massive exercise are the Electronic Voting Machines (EVMs) and Voter Verifiable Paper Audit Trails (VVPATs), safely stored in strong rooms under three-layer security. Each machine carries the fate of 2,616 candidates, representing 243 constituencies across the state.\n\nChief Electoral Officer Vinod Singh Gunjiyal told Akashvani News that stringent measures have been taken to ensure transparency and fairness. He emphasized that every counting centre is under elaborate security arrangements, ensuring a smooth and safe process.\n\nThe Election Commission of India and the Bihar administration have worked hand-in-hand to guarantee that the voice of every voter is heard without compromise.\n\nBihar’s Record-Breaking Voter Spirit\n\nThis election has been remarkable not just for its numbers but for its energy. People from every corner of Bihar — youth, women, first-time voters, and senior citizens — came together to shape the future of their state.\n\nMoreover, the enthusiasm seen in rural belts, towns, and cities alike showcases a shared dream — a better, stronger, and more empowered Bihar.\n\nFrom Gaya’s determination to Darbhanga’s drive, every ballot reflects a story of hope. As the results unfold, one thing remains certain: Bihar’s people have already won by turning up in record numbers.\n\nWhat Comes Next\n\nTomorrow’s counting will not only decide the next government but also reveal what the people of Bihar truly envision for their future. The spotlight will be on key constituencies, political veterans, and first-time contenders who represent the changing face of Bihar’s leadership.\n\nAs the results roll in, stay tuned for live updates, local reactions, and ground-level insights — only on www.biharsay.com.\n\nJoin our 13,000+ strong global community that celebrates Bihar’s progress, voices, and culture. Follow Bihar Say — Bihar’s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, reshaping the state’s image through stories of business, culture, and grassroots change.\n\nLet’s witness history together — because every vote counts, and every story matters.",
