    "id": "siwans-railway-heroes-win-safety-star-award",
    "title": "Siwan’s Railway Heroes Win Safety Star Award",
    "summary": "“Bihar Heroes on Track: Siwan’s Railway Workers Win Safety Star Award for Their Quick Action and Courage” A Spark That Could Have Been a Disaster – Saved by Bihar’s Brave Railway Workers In a state often defined by its resilience, Bihar’s Siwan district once again proved that dedication and alertness can prevent disaster. On July [...]",
    "content": "“Bihar Heroes on Track: Siwan’s Railway Workers Win Safety Star Award for Their Quick Action and Courage”\n\nA Spark That Could Have Been a Disaster – Saved by Bihar’s Brave Railway Workers\n\nIn a state often defined by its resilience, Bihar’s Siwan district once again proved that dedication and alertness can prevent disaster. On July 9, when fire broke out near the railway tracks close to Panchrukhi station, Gatekeeper Dilawar Hussain noticed the flames and acted immediately. Without hesitation, he informed the railway control room and ensured that the track was secured before any train passed. His swift decision saved lives, property, and ensured the safety of hundreds of passengers.\n\nThis act of presence of mind didn’t go unnoticed. The North Eastern Railway (NER) recognized him, along with two other Siwan-based railway workers, for their exceptional vigilance and awarded them the “Safety Star of the Month.”\n\nHonouring Bihar’s Safety Stars\n\nOn November 11, at the North Eastern Railway Headquarters in Gorakhpur, General Manager Uday Borwankar felicitated the awardees in a special ceremony. He emphasized that safety remains the top priority of Indian Railways, and employees who perform their duties with sincerity and promptness serve as true inspirations for others.\n\nAmong those honoured were:\n\nDilawar Hussain (Gateman, 83-C Siwan): Detected and reported the fire near Panchrukhi station on time.\n\nOm Prakash Kumar (Gateman, 4-C): Found a crack in the rail weld between Amalori Sarsar and Hathua on June 29 and repaired it immediately using a jogul plate.\n\nNehal Ahmad: Alerted authorities about a rail fracture at Siwan Junction on August 25, preventing a major accident.\n\nA Culture of Safety and Responsibility\n\nEvery day, thousands of trains move through Bihar’s railway network — connecting cities, villages, and livelihoods. Behind this smooth operation stand countless unsung heroes who ensure safety before speed. Their commitment transforms ordinary duties into acts of heroism.\n\nGeneral Manager Borwankar highlighted that “alert and responsible employees form the backbone of railway safety”, ensuring that millions reach their destinations safely.\n\nMore Than Just Awards — It’s About Awareness\n\nThese recognitions serve as a reminder that every alert moment counts. When employees take ownership and act promptly, they protect lives, infrastructure, and the reputation of the Railways. Bihar’s Siwan team has once again demonstrated that courage and responsibility go hand in hand.\n\n👉 For more inspiring stories like this, follow www.biharsay.com and become part of our 13K+ strong community worldwide!Bihar Say is Bihar’s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, reshaping the state’s image through stories of courage, culture, innovation, and grassroots change. Join the movement to amplify the digital voice of Bihar.",
