    "id": "bihar-election-2025-phase-2-witnessed-a-record-68-76-turnout-across-122-constituencies",
    "title": "Bihar Election 2025 Phase 2 witnessed a record 68.76% turnout across 122 constituencies",
    "summary": "Record-Breaking Bihar Votes: 68.76% Turnout Ignites Hope and High Stakes in Phase 2 Elections! Bihar Election 2025 Phase 2 Voting LIVE Updates: Historic Turnout Sparks Political Momentum Patna, Bihar: Democracy roared louder than ever in Bihar as the state witnessed a record 68.76% voter turnout during the second and final phase of the Bihar Assembly [...]",
    "content": "Record-Breaking Bihar Votes: 68.76% Turnout Ignites Hope and High Stakes in Phase 2 Elections!\n\nBihar Election 2025 Phase 2 Voting LIVE Updates: Historic Turnout Sparks Political Momentum\n\nPatna, Bihar: Democracy roared louder than ever in Bihar as the state witnessed a record 68.76% voter turnout during the second and final phase of the Bihar Assembly Elections 2025. From early morning queues to sunset selfies, the energy in polling booths reflected a new wave of civic awareness and change.\n\nThis phase holds massive significance for Chief Minister Nitish Kumar’s cabinet, as 12 ministers from his government are contesting. Every vote, therefore, carries political weight and emotional resonance.\n\nEnthusiasm Unfolds Across 122 Constituencies\n\nVoting began sharply at 7 a.m. across 122 critical constituencies spanning 20 districts. Despite a busy weekday, citizens stepped out in impressive numbers, marking one of the highest voter turnouts in Bihar’s electoral history.\n\nFrom first-time voters capturing their inked fingers to elderly citizens proudly standing in queues, Bihar’s democratic spirit was on full display. Moreover, women voters turned out in greater numbers, underscoring Bihar’s evolving political participation.\n\nTight Security and Border Sealing Amid High-Stakes Polling\n\nAs polling intensified, security forces heightened vigilance across the state. The Bihar Police, under the leadership of DGP Vinay Kumar, sealed the 700-kilometre-long international border with Nepal for 72 hours — a strong preventive step to maintain peace and order.\n\nThis decision came amid reports of heightened alert following a recent blast incident in New Delhi, prompting Bihar’s security agencies to remain proactive. Seven border districts — currently witnessing voting — are under strict monitoring, ensuring smooth conduct across polling stations.\n\nThe Pulse of Bihar: Change, Awareness, and Action\n\nEvery election in Bihar carries an emotional pulse, a sense of identity intertwined with hope. Phase 2 proved no different. Conversations around employment, education, and governance dominated public discourse, while young voters emerged as the defining force behind this historic turnout.\n\nThe emotional intensity on the ground clearly signaled one thing — Bihar is ready to redefine its future through the power of participation.\n\nWhat Lies Ahead\n\nWith the completion of Phase 2, all eyes now turn to the counting day, where numbers will decide narratives. However, beyond politics and predictions, this record turnout tells a larger story — of a state that believes, participates, and evolves.\n\nWant more real-time Bihar updates?\n\n👉 Stay tuned to www.biharsay.com for LIVE election stories, cultural insights, and inspiring ground reports.Be part of our 13K+ global community that’s redefining how the world sees Bihar — one powerful story at a time.\n\nBihar Say is Bihar’s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, reshaping the state’s image through impactful stories on culture, business, and grassroots change.With 13,000+ followers, top LinkedIn impressions, and partnerships with DailyHunt, Bihar Say stands as the digital voice of Bihar.Its flagship show, BiharCast, brings forward untold stories, changemakers, and voices from the heart of Bihar.",
