    "id": "back-to-work-after-chhath-puja-8-special-trains-from-bihar-make-return-to-delhi-mumbai-bengaluru-easier",
    "title": "Back to Work After Chhath Puja? 8 Special Trains from Bihar Make Return to Delhi, Mumbai & Bengaluru Easier",
    "summary": "The Journey Home Made Easy As the fourth day of the vibrant Chhath Puja (which concludes on 28 October) draws to a close, many festival-goers in Bihar are preparing to head back to their workplaces in other states. According to reports, 8 special trains will be deployed to ease this massive movement of people. These [...]",
    "content": "The Journey Home Made Easy\n\nAs the fourth day of the vibrant Chhath Puja (which concludes on 28 October) draws to a close, many festival-goers in Bihar are preparing to head back to their workplaces in other states. According to reports, 8 special trains will be deployed to ease this massive movement of people. These services aim to connect Bihar with major hubs like Delhi, Mumbai, Bengaluru and towns in Gujarat.\n\nWhy These 8 Special Trains Matter\n\nFirst, the holiday rush after a major festival often leads to congestion, long queues and uncertain travel. Secondly, many travellers find regular trains full or difficult to book. With dedicated special trains, travellers gain better access — including sleepers, general and AC coaches.Notably, these trains will begin operations from 28 October onwards on various routes, thereby enabling smoother return journeys from Bihar. According to local media, they will especially benefit passengers in North Bihar.\n\nWhich Trains Will Run?\n\nHere are the 8 trains announced:\n\nTrain No. 04651: Jayanagar → Amritsar (Special)\n\nTrain No. 04097: Hasanpur Road → New Delhi (Special)\n\nTrain No. 04732: Samastipur → Sriganganagar (Special)\n\nTrain No. 04449: Darbhanga → New Delhi (Special)\n\nTrain No. 07358: Raxaul → UBL (Bengaluru) Special\n\nTrain No. 05557: Raxaul → LTT (Mumbai) Special\n\nTrain No. 09068: Jayanagar → Udhna Special\n\nTrain No. 09070: Samastipur → Udhna Special\n\nBy introducing these routes, the rail network expands relief and return-options for those heading back to metros and industrial hubs.\n\nWhat to Keep in Mind Before Boarding\n\nBook early: Seats are limited and with the festival rush, availability drops fast.\n\nCheck class options: These specials include AC, Sleeper and General—so pick what suits you.\n\nRoutes and timings: They vary by origin and destination; verify schedule ahead of travel.\n\nExtra coaches may be added: Officials say extra coaches will be attached if demand surges.\n\nPlan arrival to main hubs: Whether you’re going to Delhi, Mumbai or Bengaluru, ensure onward connectivity.\n\nWhy This Move Matters for Bihar Travellers\n\nBy launching these specials, the railways recognise the massive travel demand from Bihar during Chhath and other festivals. For many from Bihar working in metro cities, the return journey often is fraught with uncertainty. Thanks to this move:\n\nIt offers better connectivity between Bihar and major employment centres.\n\nIt shows a responsive transport policy, matching travel peak with supply.\n\nIt helps families return home, celebrate, and then go back without undue delay.\n\nStay Informed, Stay Ahead\n\nWant daily updates on Bihar’s infrastructure, transit news and transport developments? Follow www.biharsay.com for real-time stories. Join our 13K+ global community and be part of Bihar’s transformation through stories on culture, business and grassroots change. 👉 Visit now and never miss a beat!",
