    "id": "166-additional-flights-to-patna-for-diwali-chhath-2025",
    "title": "166 Additional Flights to Patna for Diwali & Chhath 2025",
    "summary": "Patna Welcomes 166 Extra Flights for Diwali & Chhath Puja This festive season, Patna is set to become the travel hotspot of Bihar. Air India and its subsidiary Air India Express have announced a massive addition of 166 extra flights to meet soaring travel demand during Diwali and Chhath Puja. Consequently, passengers traveling from key [...]",
    "content": "Patna Welcomes 166 Extra Flights for Diwali & Chhath Puja\n\nThis festive season, Patna is set to become the travel hotspot of Bihar. Air India and its subsidiary Air India Express have announced a massive addition of 166 extra flights to meet soaring travel demand during Diwali and Chhath Puja. Consequently, passengers traveling from key cities like Delhi, Mumbai, and Bengaluru can now enjoy more convenient schedules and smoother connections.\n\nThe additional flights begin operations October 15, 2025, and continue until November 3, 2025. Therefore, travelers should plan early to secure their seats and avoid last-minute hassles.\n\nAir India: Expanded Routes and Numbers\n\nAir India will operate 114 additional flights to Patna. Specifically:\n\nDelhi–Patna: 38 extra flights\n\nMumbai–Patna: 38 extra flights\n\nBengaluru–Patna: 38 extra flights\n\nMoreover, these flights complement the existing 42 weekly Air India flights from Delhi and Mumbai. As a result, passengers have more flexibility to choose their preferred travel times.\n\nAir India Express Enhances Festive Connectivity\n\nSimilarly, Air India Express adds 52 flights between October 22 and November 3, 2025:\n\nDelhi–Patna: 26 additional flights\n\nBengaluru–Patna: 26 additional flights\n\nAdditionally, these flights supplement the current 14 weekly Air India Express flights. Therefore, the festive travel rush is expected to ease considerably, offering passengers more convenient options.\n\nSmooth Connections to Domestic and International Destinations\n\nFurthermore, these additional flights not only boost domestic connectivity but also facilitate seamless transfers to international destinations via Delhi, Mumbai, and Bengaluru hubs. Consequently, travelers heading to the Middle East or Europe can coordinate layovers efficiently.\n\nThis expansion is particularly helpful for Biharis living abroad who wish to celebrate Diwali and Chhath with their families. Indeed, the move reflects the airlines’ commitment to serving passengers’ festive travel needs while minimizing congestion and delays.\n\nHow to Book Your Festive Flight\n\nBooking for these flights is now open through multiple channels:\n\nOfficial websites and mobile apps of Air India and Air India Express\n\n24×7 contact centres\n\nCity and airport ticketing offices\n\nTravel agents worldwide\n\nHence, passengers can choose the most convenient booking method and ensure a smooth festive journey.\n\nStay updated with the latest travel news and festive announcements by following Bihar Say. Become part of our 13,000+ strong global community, and enjoy regular insights on Bihar’s culture, business, and grassroots changes. Bihar Say is reshaping the state’s narrative with stories that matter, and you can be part of this journey today!",
